          "id": "lifecycle-serialize-copy-null",
          "change_ids": [],
          "kind": "lifecycle",
          "necessary": true,
          "established": true,
          "requirement": "A successfully loaded item must retain valid allocator accounting through serialization, and the entry must not dereference a failed copy.",
          "target_route": "Supply a valid definite byte string of 400,000,000 bytes: header 0x5A 0x17 0xD7 0x84 0x00 followed by 400,000,000 data bytes. cbor_load copies the data, cbor_serialize_alloc allocates another 400,000,005 bytes, the entry frees that buffer with plain free, then calls cbor_copy.",
          "failure_condition": "The tracked total still includes the freed serialization buffer. Copying the byte string requests another 400,000,000 bytes, which exceeds the 1 GiB tracked limit; cbor_copy returns NULL and the entry passes that NULL to cbor_decref, which dereferences it.",
          "alternative_paths": "The complete entry has no accounting release between free(buffer) and cbor_copy, no check of copied before cbor_decref, and no alternative copy route. Using limited_free for the serialization buffer would remove its tracked size.",
